  "name": "AP – Drive intake",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-drive-intake",
      "name": "Note: Drive intake",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "content": "## Drive intake\nTurns files dropped in the Google Drive folder **AP Automation/Inbox** into processed invoices, through the same core as email: same extraction, checks, duplicate detection and review.\n\nn8n lists the folder and moves the files. The **core service decides** which files to process, the status, and what a failure means. The AI only extracts data; every decision is deterministic code.",
        "height": 350,
        "width": 1620
      },
      "position": [
        -40,
        -150
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-find-folders",
      "name": "Note: Find folders",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Find folders\nEvery minute: finds **AP Automation** and its **Inbox**, **Processed** and **Error** folders. Missing ones are created (the subfolders on the run after a new AP Automation); processing starts on the next run.",
        "height": 550,
        "width": 900
      },
      "position": [
        -40,
        250
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-screen-core",
      "name": "Note: Screen (core)",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Screen (core)\nThe Inbox is the queue. The core answers per file: **process** now, **wait** (being processed, retry not due, or next run), or **error** (not a PDF or image, too large, given up: logged).",
        "height": 350,
        "width": 1140
      },
      "position": [
        920,
        250
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-process-core",
      "name": "Note: Process (core)",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Process (core)\nDownload, then extract, normalize, check, store: the same endpoint as email (source **drive:<file ID>**). The same file already received by email is an exact duplicate.",
        "height": 350,
        "width": 660
      },
      "position": [
        2120,
        250
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-move,-then-post",
      "name": "Note: Move, then post",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Move, then post\nAny status (ready, needs review, rejected) → **Processed**; ready invoices start the posting workflow. A file the core refuses (too large, not really a PDF or image) → **Error**.",
        "height": 550,
        "width": 660
      },
      "position": [
        2840,
        250
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-technical-error",
      "name": "Note: Technical error",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "content": "## Technical error\nDownload or processing failed (e.g. OCR service down, core unreachable): logged and reported to the core. Temporary → the file stays in **Inbox** and is retried when due (15 min, 1 h, 4 h, 12 h). Permanent, or 5 attempts used → **given up**, moved to **Error**: a person looks.",
        "height": 350,
        "width": 900
      },
      "position": [
        2120,
        850
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
